// An array as a value, kept methods: casts: `method int h() { return a } method int g() { int r = 0 for (int j = 0; j
// < 2; j++) { r += h() } return r } initial state A do x = g() go to A`. KIELER rejects it: assignment to ‘int’ from
// ‘int *’ makes integer from pointer without a cast [-Wint-conversion].
scchart Main { input bool b input int i int a[2] = {4,7} int c[2] = {4,7} int m[2][2] = {{4,7},{8,1}} float fa[2] bool ba[2] output int x output float f output bool y method int h() { return a } method int g() { int r = 0 for (int j = 0; j < 2; j++) { r += h() } return r } initial state A do x = g() go to A }
